From: Hoki local development <code@lukasrieger.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCM: account for actual synchronous playback write lengths

PulseAudio issues sub-period writes. Count the submitted length on DSP
completion, preserve pre-RUN lengths, and retain ring-position overshoot.
Snapshot completed length before recycling the DSP slot. Rebuild the entire
audio module set because the shared internal structures change.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/asoc/msm-pcm-q6-v2.c
+++ b/asoc/msm-pcm-q6-v2.c
@@ -156,6 +156,13 @@
 	}
 }
 
+static void msm_pcm_advance(struct msm_audio *prtd, unsigned int bytes)
+{
+	if (prtd->pcm_size)
+		WRITE_ONCE(prtd->pcm_irq_pos,
+			(READ_ONCE(prtd->pcm_irq_pos) + bytes) % prtd->pcm_size);
+}
